From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:06:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 61/61] Arabic liveness texts reviewed by a native speaker:
 polite, gender-neutral instructions (task 27)

The Arabic review of 2026-10-28 (both batches). The liveness term is confirmed correct by the reviewer.
The main point: direct masculine commands become the polite, gender-neutral "please + noun" form used by
most other texts. Texts are taken from the reviewer's files, not retyped.
- The 9 corrections (rows marked N): liveness_challenge_blink, feedback_hold_still, error_device_problem,
  tips_look_at_camera, tips_face_visible, tips_lighting, tips_capture_area, tips_follow_prompt,
  model_select_file.
- Optional suggestions adopted: liveness_status_passed (a photo of your face, as in Hindi and Kannada);
  liveness_model_installed in the future tense. Consistency: liveness_model_rolled_back in the future tense too.
- The word for "resident" stays: MOSIP's own Arabic texts use the same word.
- No direct masculine command remains. The review notes of app_ar.arb record the review: all five
  translated languages are now reviewed.

Tests: liveness_l10n_test and model_bundle_test (the review note), liveness_page_locale_test (the new
look-at-camera tip). flutter test test/liveness: 325 passing, 20 skipped (the Arabic layout and
right-to-left checks at 360 and 412 dp among them).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
